{"name":"Synchronicity","hex":"#c7d4ce","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"synchronicity","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The state of being synchronous or simultaneous.","Coincidences that seem to be meaningfully related; supposedly the result of \"universal forces\"."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/synchronicity"}],"entries":[{"title":"Synchronicity","blocks":[{"text":"Synchronicity is a concept introduced by Carl Jung, founder of analytical psychology, to describe events that coincide in time and appear meaningfully related, yet lack a discoverable causal connection. Jung held that this was a healthy function of the mind, although it can become harmful within psychosis."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Greek_uc_psi_icon.svg/330px-Greek_uc_psi_icon.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Synchronicity"},{"title":"Synchronicity (The Police album)","blocks":[{"text":"Synchronicity is the fifth and final studio album by the English rock band the Police, released on 17 June 1983 by A&M Records. The band's most successful release, the album includes the hit singles \"Every Breath You Take\", \"King of Pain\", \"Wrapped Around Your Finger\", and \"Synchronicity II\". The album's title and much of the material for the songs were inspired by Arthur Koestler's book The Roots of Coincidence (1972). At the 1984 Grammy Awards the album was nominated for a total of five awards, including Album of the Year, and won three. At the time of its release and following the Synchronicity Tour, the Police's popularity was at such a high that they were arguably, according to BBC and The Guardian, the \"biggest band in the world\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7f/Police-album-synchronicity.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Synchronicity_(The_Police_album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/CGJung.jpg/500px-CGJung.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/CGJung.jpg/1280px-CGJung.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/CGJung.jpg/500px-CGJung.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Carl G. Jung, who coined the term synchronicity between 1928 and 1930","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACGJung.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Wolfgang_Pauli_ETH-Bib_Portr_01042_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Wolfgang_Pauli_ETH-Bib_Portr_01042_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Wolfgang_Pauli_ETH-Bib_Portr_01042_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Wolfgang_Pauli_ETH-Bib_Portr_01042_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wolfgang Pauli","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWolfgang_Pauli_ETH-Bib_Portr_01042_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Brescia_Piazza_della_Loggia_Torre_dell%27Orologio_Ziffernblatt_4.jpg/500px-Brescia_Piazza_della_Loggia_Torre_dell%27Orologio_Ziffernblatt_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Brescia_Piazza_della_Loggia_Torre_dell%27Orologio_Ziffernblatt_4.jpg/1280px-Brescia_Piazza_della_Loggia_Torre_dell%27Orologio_Ziffernblatt_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Brescia_Piazza_della_Loggia_Torre_dell%27Orologio_Ziffernblatt_4.jpg/500px-Brescia_Piazza_della_Loggia_Torre_dell%27Orologio_Ziffernblatt_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Astral configurations in astrology represent for Jung an example of synchronicity, that is, of a parallel, non-causal relationship between the development of celestial phenomena and those marked by terrestrial time.[42][43]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrescia_Piazza_della_Loggia_Torre_dell'Orologio_Ziffernblatt_4.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Cetonia_aurata_MF.jpg/500px-Cetonia_aurata_MF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Cetonia_aurata_MF.jpg/1280px-Cetonia_aurata_MF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Cetonia_aurata_MF.jpg/500px-Cetonia_aurata_MF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A gold-coloured Cetonia aurata","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACetonia_aurata_MF.jpg"}],"sounds":{"synchronicity":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d7/En-us-synchronicity.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/d/d7/En-us-synchronicity.ogg/En-us-synchronicity.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/46/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Rho9998-synchronicity.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/46/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Rho9998-synchronicity.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Rho9998-synchronicity.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transc